# Python Port Plan — Step 05: The Agent Loop

## Goal

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/05_agent_loop` to
`week1_baseline/python/05_agent_loop`. This is the step where everything
prior (structs, registry, prompt builder, client) gets wired into an actual
agent loop: `Agent#run` sends a request, checks the normalized
`stop_reason`, dispatches any tool calls via the `Registry`, feeds the
results back, and repeats — up to a configurable `max_iterations` ceiling,
after which it makes one tools-disabled "wind-down" call instead of raising.
Every backend gains a `parse_response` (raw response → common shape) and,
where needed, an inverse `assistant_message`/`assistant_parts` (common shape
→ provider-specific replay format). Also adds `Tasks::Base.max_iterations`/
`.max_output_tokens`, a (currently unused) `LoopError`, and `tools:`
passthrough on `PromptBuilder`/`Client`/each backend's `to_payload`.

**⚠️ Bigger safety note than step 4.** `example.py` will run a real,
multi-turn agentic loop against the live Anthropic API (per current
`settings.yaml`) — not just one request. It registers real `read_file`/
`list_directory` tools scoped to the port's own directory, and the loop can
make up to `max_iterations` (default 25, but realistically 1-3 for this
task) real billed round-trips, actually reading files and listing
directories under `python/05_agent_loop/` for real. Confirm before running
during implementation/testing, the same way step 4 was confirmed.

